Shanling Q2 tools
=================

q2-jellyfin runs from the card's .jellyfin folder as a Q2 Pod card app (q2-pod's patch/addon.c): a
Jellyfin client that syncs and streams. Forked from q2-subsonic (MIT), itself built from q2-filebrowser's scripts.

  build.sh     static Go for the Q2 and the card files, in target/shanlingq2/.jellyfin, zipped as
               target/shanlingq2/q2-jellyfin-vX.Y-SHA.zip (unzip that at the card's root)
  package.py   checks the binary (static, MIPS32 little-endian, soft-float ABI), sets the nan2008
               ELF flag the Q2's kernel requires and Go doesn't, and writes the ZIP
  launcher.sh  installed as .jellyfin/run: q2-jellyfin copied to /tmp and run there in a restart loop
  q2app        installed as .jellyfin/q2app: the card app manifest (name=Jellyfin, qr=0; stop=0: no
               Stop Jellyfin row, Cancel on an error page; more=npqueue Play Queue: Now Playing's ⋯
               on Jellyfin's queue opens the songs queued; favdir=Jellyfin)
  icon.png, icon-40.png
               Streaming's row icon, 52 px (Legacy) and 40 px (iPod): the Jellyfin logo in its
               colours (CC BY-SA 4.0, see NOTICE); Q2 Pod greys it in the Minimal theme
  icons.py     draws the two icons from Jellyfin's icon-transparent.svg (Pillow)
  test_launcher.py
               runs launcher.sh on the host with a fake app
